BrowserJDK licensing scope
==========================

BrowserJDK's native and Java runtime glue under src/native and src/java is
licensed under GNU General Public License version 2 only, with the Classpath
Exception below. The independent JavaScript OJ adapter under src/js is
licensed under the MIT License below.

OpenJDK source and port changes retain the license header of each modified
file. The Classpath Exception applies only where the corresponding upstream
file explicitly says that it applies. No exception is added to a file that
does not already carry it.

The complete GPLv2 text is contained in the pinned OpenJDK source tree and is
copied verbatim into every generated binary distribution's LICENSE file. The
corresponding source bundle contains that exact source tree and license.

Classpath Exception
-------------------

Linking this library statically or dynamically with other modules is making a
combined work based on this library. Thus, the terms and conditions of the GNU
General Public License cover the whole combination.

As a special exception, the copyright holders of this library give you
permission to link this library with independent modules to produce an
executable, regardless of the license terms of these independent modules, and
to copy and distribute the resulting executable under terms of your choice,
provided that you also meet, for each linked independent module, the terms and
conditions of the license of that module. An independent module is a module
which is not derived from or based on this library. If you modify this library,
you may extend this exception to your version of the library, but you are not
obligated to do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete this exception statement
from your version.

